{"agent":"lane-lock","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`renewer` only returns a callable and merge invokes it twice, both before the blocking `W.merge`. Nothing renews on an interval while that call runs, and nothing is stopped when it returns. With a short lease TTL, a merge that takes longer than the TTL (the 10-minute case in the acceptance) lets the lease expire mid-merge; a waiter can take the item or the holder loses it, which is the failure this change was supposed to close. The new test only counts that the spy lambda was called at t=0, so it stays green when the lease dies during `W.merge`.","digest":"909e63e2a1349384","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/merge.py:315","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/merge.py:315"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_no_renewal` succeeds only when `gone.state` is `DONE` or `ABANDONED`. A released item is neither: claim then release, then `heartbeat` on that id. Control falls through to `L.renew`, which is the old failure (`no lease held`, exit non-zero) or, if a stale lease record is still live, an extension. The contract requires that case to return success and not touch the lease. The new test never releases an item, so it does not catch this.","digest":"be5ca485b2a7e032","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/heartbeat.py:92","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/heartbeat.py:92"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The accepted behavior also requires `doctor` to list heartbeat-looking processes whose item is already finished (pid and command line) and the pkill hook to say how to stop them. This change never touches doctor or that hook. After a finished item, a leftover heartbeat process is invisible to `doctor`, so the operator has no listing to act on.","digest":"708d2a4c37242a71","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/leasekeep.py:41","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/leasekeep.py:41"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":8110,"diff_sha":"461c26ba65cb444a0e0ab6df7740e142c28fb9f2472e4cba8ef76d5294f62c47","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/LK-auto-heartbeat","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":131.7,"family":"xai","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"2f03ddac11f4c62c","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/LK-auto-heartbeat.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261111T220302Z-a9f9d004.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"6f1a210e43a9b434dd002d4ef567c806a0e4abcb","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/lifecycle/heartbeat.py":"100644 fc2d08e3b57093ceeb71d70b2e82c3c10413fc0c","ddflow/api/lifecycle/merge.py":"100644 48135542cf464491fc5999d1a46a0f0e92baa6a4","ddflow/services/leasekeep.py":"100644 a5a6931c0d850d8918c747cb86652377ce57540b","tests/test_auto_heartbeat.py":"100644 8b87f7375e163b2eefc32194dfce8d2d3b08e0d7"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/lifecycle/merge.py:315","ddflow/api/lifecycle/heartbeat.py:92","ddflow/services/leasekeep.py:41"],"tree_sha":"6f1a210e43a9+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"3 finding(s)"},"id":"ee6c7eac20df06ab296feaa70","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":177925,"schema":1,"subject":"LK-auto-heartbeat","ts":"2026-11-11T22:05:24.004281Z"}
